        "original_id": "ae9cb842-5fb2-5ae3-b0b5-f85b8d6aa81a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Willunga, Adelaide, southern Adelaide suburbs, Adelaide CBD\n- Systems: Willunga railway line, Gawler line\n- Organizations: Adelaide railway station, City of Onkaparinga\n- Topics: distance, population\n\nFacts:\n- The Willunga railway line ran from Adelaide railway station through the southern Adelaide suburbs to Willunga.\n- The Willunga railway line was over 45 km long.\n- The Gawler line is 42.2 km long.\n- Willunga is a town south of Adelaide in South Australia.\n- Willunga is in the City of Onkaparinga local government area.\n- Willunga is 47 km from the Adelaide CBD.\n- At the 2011 census, Willunga had a population of 2,416.",
